    "type": "numeric",
    "prompt": "Given $\\triangle ABC$, $D$ and $E$ are on $\\overline{BC}$ such that $\\overline{AD}$ bisects $\\angle BAC$ and $\\overline{AE}$ bisects $\\angle CAD$. If $m\\angle ABC : m\\angle AEB : m\\angle ACB = 5 : 2 : 1$, compute $m\\angle ADC + m\\angle AEC$ in degrees.",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "270",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Angle chasing",
        "body": "Let $m\\angle BAC=4x$, so $m\\angle BAD=m\\angle DAC=2x$ and $m\\angle DAE=m\\angle EAC=x$. Let $m\\angle ABC=5y$, $m\\angle AEB=2y$, $m\\angle ACB=y$.\n\n$\\angle AEB$ is an exterior angle of $\\triangle AEC$, so $2y=x+y$, giving $x=y$. The angles of $\\triangle ABC$ give $4x+5y+y=180^\\circ$, so $x=y=18^\\circ$.\n\nIn $\\triangle ADC$: $m\\angle ADC=180^\\circ-2x-y=180^\\circ-54^\\circ=126^\\circ$.\n\nIn $\\triangle AEC$: $m\\angle AEC=180^\\circ-x-y=144^\\circ$.\n\nSum: $126^\\circ+144^\\circ=270^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: 270**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
