      {
        "title": "Match prime factors",
        "body": "RHS: $12^3=2^6\\cdot3^3$, $14^C=2^C\\cdot7^C$, $15^5=3^5\\cdot5^5$. So RHS $=2^{6+C}\\cdot3^8\\cdot5^5\\cdot7^C$. Matching: $A=6+C$, $B=5$, $4=C$. Thus $C=4$, $A=10$, $B=5$. $(A,B,C)=(10,5,4)$."
      }
