    "choices": null,
    "answer": "1",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Substitute y=x-1",
        "body": "Let $y=x-1$, $x=y+1$. Expanding $(y+1)^3-4(y+1)^2+7(y+1)-6=y^3-y^2+2y-2$. By Vieta's on the new polynomial: $\\sum 1/y_i = (\\text{sum of products of pairs})/(\\text{product})=2/2=1$."
