    "prompt": "A \\\"tic-tac-toe\\\" consists of having the same symbol in three consecutive squares of an array (this may be horizontally, vertically, or diagonally). An array has three rows of four squares. If X's are placed at random in three different squares, compute the probability that the X's will form a \\\"tic-tac-toe\\\".",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "7/110",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count favorable arrangements",
        "body": "Total: $\\binom{12}{3}=220$. Horizontal (3 consecutive in a row of 4): 2 sets per row $\\times$ 3 rows = 6. Vertical (3 in a column of 3): 4 columns = 4. Diagonal: 2 going right-down + 2 going left-down = 4. Total favorable = 6+4+4=14. $P=14/220=7/110$."
      }
    ],
