    "prompt": "The line with slope $m$ bisects the acute angle between the lines $y = x$ and $y = 2x$. The value of $m$ may be expressed in simplest form as $\\dfrac{a+\\sqrt{b}}{c}$ for integers $a$, $b$ and $c$. Compute the ordered triple $(a, b, c)$.",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "$(1, 10, 3)$",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Angle bisector condition",
        "body": "The angle bisector between lines with slopes 1 and 2 has slope $m$ satisfying $\\left|\\frac{1-m}{1+m}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{2-m}{1+2m}\\right|$. Taking the case that gives a slope between 1 and 2: $3m^2-2m-3=0$, $m=\\frac{2+\\sqrt{40}}{6}=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{10}}{3}$. So $(a,b,c)=(1,10,3)$."
      }
