        "body": "Place $RA$ on the $y$-axis: $A=(0,0)$, $R=(0,6)$. Since $TP\\parallel RA$, $T$ and $P$ share an $x$-coordinate $d$. From $AP=13$: $d^2+p_y^2=169$; $TR=15$: $d^2+(t_y-6)^2=225$; $TP=20$: $t_y-p_y=20$. Solving: $p_y=-5$, $t_y=15$, $d=12$. Area of trapezoid: $\\frac{1}{2}(6+20)\\cdot12=156$. Centroid distance from axis: $\\bar{x}=\\frac{d}{3}\\cdot\\frac{a+2b}{a+b}=\\frac{12}{3}\\cdot\\frac{6+40}{26}=\\frac{92}{13}$. Volume: $2\\pi\\bar{x}\\cdot A=2\\pi\\cdot\\frac{92}{13}\\cdot156=2208\\pi$."
      }
    ],
