    "prompt": "Compute the number of real solutions of the equation $\\log x = 2\\cos x$.",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "31",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count crossings period by period",
        "body": "Here $\\log$ is base $10$. Since $|2\\cos x|\\le2$, solutions need $-2\\le\\log x\\le2$, i.e. $0.01\\le x\\le100$.\n\nOn $(0,2\\pi]$, $\\log x<0.8$ while $2\\cos x$ falls from $2$ to $-2$ and rises back to $2$, so the graphs cross twice (once on the downswing, once on the upswing). The same happens on each interval $[2k\\pi,2(k+1)\\pi]$ for $k=0,1,\\dots,14$, since $\\log x<2$ there ($30\\pi\\approx94.2<100$). That gives $2\\cdot15=30$ intersections.\n\nOn $[30\\pi,100]$, $2\\cos x$ starts at $2>\\log x$ and decreases, giving one more crossing; it does not climb back above $\\log x$ before $x=100$ (the next peak is at $32\\pi>100$, where $\\log x>2$ anyway).\n\nTotal: $30+1=31$.\n\n**Answer: 31**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "algebra",
      "trigonometry"
    ],
