      {
        "title": "Law of sines",
        "body": "$\\sin T=3/5$, $\\cos T=4/5$; $\\sin N=15/17$, $\\cos N=8/17$. $\\sin A=\\sin(T+N)=\\sin T\\cos N+\\cos T\\sin N=\\frac{24}{85}+\\frac{60}{85}=\\frac{84}{85}$. By law of sines: $\\frac{TA}{\\sin N}=\\frac{TN}{\\sin A}$, so $\\frac{TA}{TN}=\\frac{\\sin N}{\\sin A}=\\frac{15/17}{84/85}=\\frac{75}{84}=\\frac{25}{28}$."
